        <mxCell id="a_v30" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; lifecycle_state (where the loan is) and AssessmentResult.assurance_state (what the evidence says) are separate attributes of separate classes (ES-04: HELD_FOR_REVIEW with REVIEW_RECOMMENDED).&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; BorrowingTransaction is rebuilt only through apply(); nothing sets lifecycle_state directly (FR-B-09).&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Student 2 implements AssuranceEngine and OutcomeSink; Student 1 implements IndirectTrustEngine, which the AssuranceEngine calls through IIndirectEvidence.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Module 9 (Student 3) calls BorrowingService.apply_decision() through ILifecycleCommands; it is not drawn here.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Relationship ends: &amp;#9670; composition, &amp;#9671; aggregation, dashed open arrow = dependency, dashed hollow triangle = realisation.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; &lt;font color='#0A7A36'&gt;Green&lt;/font&gt; = added or changed in iteration 2; the scheduler (JobRunner) calls BorrowingService like any user command." style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=10.5;fontStyle=0;fontColor=#1d1d1d;spacing=2;overflow=visible;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="1384" width="500" height="258" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
